    <h2>Scan, don’t gag</h2>
    <p>Our 3D scanner is a small wand that takes thousands of pictures of your teeth in a few minutes. No trays of putty, no gagging, and you can watch your teeth appear on the screen as we go. The same scan lets you see a simulation of how your teeth might move.</p>
    <h2>Living with aligners</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Wear them about 22 hours a day: the time out is for meals and brushing.</li>
        <li>Carry the case. Wrapping aligners in a napkin is how most of them get lost.</li>
        <li>Clean them gently with cool water and a soft brush, never hot water.</li>
        <li>Check in every six to ten weeks. Wednesday evenings are kept for aligner patients.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Honest advice</h2>
    <p>Not everyone needs aligners. If your teeth are healthy and your bite works, Dr. Castellano will say so. Read his thoughts in <a href="/blog/clear-aligners-honest-guide/">an honest guide to clear aligners</a>.</p>
